    "body": "## Summary\n\nCommit 1 of ADR-030: flip table + skip-link hide. **Closes three of the four remaining first-viewport bugs** from ADR-029's live visual verification.\n\n## The visible delta\n\nMeasured on Wikipedia at viewport 1774:\n\n| Element | Before ADR-030 | After ADR-030 | Delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `.vector-page-toolbar` height | 687 | **~40-60** | **−650** |\n| Read/View/View history y | ~4873 | **~180** | **−4693** |\n| `vector-body` (article intro) y | 834 | **~250-350** | **−500** |\n| \"Jump to content\" skip link | visible | **hidden** | — |\n| `h1#firstHeading` y | 107 | 107 | unchanged |\n| `.mw-page-container-inner` y | 59 | 59 | unchanged |\n\n## What the first viewport now shows\n\nThe PNG (rendered from the new pipeline) confirms:\n\n- Compact header bar — Donate / Create account / Log in right-aligned\n- **\"HTML\" article title** prominent at top\n- Article / Talk tabs with **Read / View source / View history inline**\n- \"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\"\n- **Intro paragraph**: \"Markup language for documents\" + the multiple-issues maintenance banners\n- No Tools panel\n- No skip link\n\n**Article content is above the fold for the first time.**\n\n## What changed\n\n### 1. Flip table refactor\n\n`apply_viewport_feature_classes()` moves from one hardcoded `main-menu-pinned` flip to a `constexpr FeatureFlip kDesktopFeatureFlips[]` table:\n\n- `main-menu-pinned` (ADR-029) — mobile hamburger menu 711px → 0\n- `page-tools-pinned` (ADR-030) — Tools panel 687px → hidden\n\nSame 1120 threshold, same idempotent round-trip semantics. Future flips add one entry per line — no code duplication.\n\n**Not flipped** (intentional): `clientpref-*` flags (toc-pinned, limited-width, custom-font-size, appearance-pinned). These are user preferences that real Wikipedia reads from `localStorage` at load. We have no `localStorage`, and flipping them would override server-side defaults. Left alone.\n\n### 2. Skip-link hide\n\n`.mw-jump-link { display: none !important }` injected into `viewport_css` at desktop.\n\nReal Wikipedia uses `.mw-jump-link:not(:focus) { position: absolute; clip: rect(1px,1px,1px,1px); overflow: hidden; }` — four unimplemented CSS features (`:not`, `position: absolute`, `clip`, and eventually `:focus`). The `!important` override beats the `.mw-jump-link:not(:focus)` rule (which our matcher can't reach — no `:not()` support).\n\n**Will be removed when ADR-031 lands** — the proper visually-hidden pattern will take over, and `:focus` support (future ADR) will make the link Tab-reachable.\n\n## The scope split, honest\n\nADR-030 was originally planned as `position` + `:checked`. Measurement showed the visible bugs were driven by **feature-class flags**, not by position/`:checked` — 47 `position` rules and 14 `:checked` rules in Wikipedia's CSS but none of them direct drivers of the four visible bugs.\n\nSo: ADR-030 = flip table + skip-link hide (~20 lines). ADR-031 = the structural `position` + `:checked` + `:not` + `clip` work (~300-400 lines), needed for future features (dropdowns that open on click, infoboxes, thumbnails, sticky headers).\n\nThe measurement earned the reframe. Small change, small risk, largest visible delta.\n\n## Two honest observations deferred\n\n1. **Infobox renders as inline list** (`.html / .htm / text/html / WHATWG / …` stacked at bottom of first viewport) instead of the top-right `float: right` box. `float` not implemented. ADR-031 candidate.\n2. **Stray `</html>`** in the top-right corner of the viewport. A small parser leak — not introduced by this commit. Deferred to its own note.\n\nNeither regresses any prior ADR. Both documented for future cycles.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-030: 394 cases / 1643 assertions\n- After Commit 1: **399 cases / 1660 assertions** (+5 / +17)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Flip table refactor preserves ADR-029 main-menu flip | ✅ |\n| `page-tools-pinned` flips at desktop | ✅ |\n| `page-tools-pinned` unchanged at mobile | ✅ |\n| Both flips round-trip on resize | ✅ |\n| `.mw-jump-link` hidden at desktop | ✅ |\n| `.mw-jump-link` untouched at mobile | ✅ |\n| Wikipedia first-viewport visual | ✅ (PNG) |\n| No regression to prior ADRs | ✅ |\n| Full suite green | ✅ |\n\nRefs #166\n",
